  "review_findings": [
    {
      "topic": "One page per drain",
      "assessment": "Serial and revocation call exactly once before their claim loops. Parallel calls exactly once before worker construction; no per-worker/per-claim multiplier. Budget is min(max_batch,64)."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Target isolation and progress",
      "assessment": "space_id, claimed state and expiry predicates occur inside the ORDER BY task_id LIMIT selection;193 earlier foreign tasks cannot absorb a target page. Repeated explicit drains progress137 target rows64/64/9/0; production runtime uses max_batch16 and its existing full-batch continuation remains aligned with the page bound."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Transactions and row semantics",
      "assessment": "One write mutex and BEGIN IMMEDIATE cover selection/update/exhaustion read/commit. Both statement/query error and commit failure issue rollback. Reclaim preserves attempt_count and last_error, clears lease token/deadline/owner, updates availability, and performs no epoch effect. Token fencing stays in unchanged claim/publish consumers."
    },
    {
      "topic": "No early-expiry or terminal revival",
      "assessment": "Strict lease_expires_at < now and state=claimed constrain mutation. Real-clock control observes0 before deadline and1 after real elapsed expiry; long lease, foreign rows, future pending rows, failed and superseded rows are byte-protected in fixtures."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Cancellation and active-space boundary",
      "assessment": "Already-closed lifecycle and missing active space return before reclaim; existing per-claim cancellation/lifecycle guards remain. Parallel retains active-space-change refusal. No new atomic cancellation guarantee between the early check and the auxiliary DB transaction is claimed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "API compatibility",
      "assessment": "Legacy global bounded and unbounded APIs retain exact old bytes. New DB API rejects0 and usize values outside positive i64 before SQLite LIMIT, preventing negative LIMIT overflow. Public existing claim/retry budgets and attempt rules are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Validation scope",
      "assessment": "Real SQLite mutations observed through an independent audit trigger; rows deliberately aged are explicitly synthetic fixture data, not SIGKILL evidence. Existing L3 crash driver is separate. No claim of bounded SQL scan time, release SLA, full quality certification, or independent product execution by this reviewer."
    }
  ],
